== Stage 12 ==
;16 July 2026 – [[Circuit de Nevers Magny-Cours]] to [[Chalon-sur-Saône]], {{convert|179.1|km|abbr=on}}
The twelfth stage of the stage took riders eastwards from [[Circuit de Nevers Magny-Cours]] to [[Chalon-sur-Saône]], over a flat {{convert|179.1|km|abbr=on}} course with three fourth-category climbs.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Stage 12 - Circuit Nevers Magny-Cours > Chalon-sur-Saône - Tour de France 2026 |url=https://www.letour.fr/en/stage-12 |access-date=2026-07-05 |website=www.letour.fr |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite book |title=2026 Tour de France Roadbook |publisher=Amaury Sport Organisation |pages=118, 120}}</ref>

Merlier won stage 12 in a sprint finish despite a large crash behind. Pedersen remained in the green jersey of the points classification, slowly extending his lead.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Whittle |first=Jeremy |date=2026-07-16 |title=Tim Merlier surges to Tour de France 2026 hat-trick on stage 12 but crash hits sprinters |url=https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/jul/16/tim-merlier-tour-de-france-2026-hat-trick-stage-12-crash-hits-sprinters-cycling |access-date=2026-07-24 |work=The Guardian |language=en-GB |issn=0261-3077}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Ostanek |first=Dani |date=2026-07-16 |title=Tour de France: Tim Merlier wins sprint skirmish on stage 12 ahead of major pileup |url=https://www.cyclingnews.com/pro-cycling/racing/tour-de-france-tim-merlier-wins-sprint-skirmish-on-stage-12-ahead-of-major-pileup/ |access-date=2026-07-24 |website=Cyclingnews |language=en}}</ref>

