== Stage 15 ==
;19 July 2026 – [[Champagnole]] to [[Col de Solaison|Plateau de Solaison]], {{convert|183.9|km|abbr=on}}
Moving south to the mountains in the [[Jura Mountains|Jura]] and [[French Alps]], stage 15 took riders from [[Champagnole]] to a summit finish at [[Col de Solaison|Plateau de Solaison]] over a {{convert|183.9|km|abbr=on}} course.<ref name=":2" /><ref name=":3">{{Cite book |title=2026 Tour de France Roadbook |publisher=Amaury Sport Organisation |pages=146, 148, 151}}</ref> Four categorised climbs were featured – two third-category climbs, the first-category Le Salève - Col de la Croisette (4.6&nbsp;km at an average gradient of 11.2%) and the ''[[hors catégorie]]'' ascent to the summit finish at Plateau de Solaison (11.3&nbsp;km at an average gradient of 9%, with the finish at an elevation of {{convert|1508|m|ft|abbr=on}}).<ref name=":2">{{Cite web |title=Stage 15 - Champagnole > Plateau de Solaison - Tour de France 2026 |url=https://www.letour.fr/en/stage-15 |access-date=2026-07-05 |website=www.letour.fr |language=en}}</ref><ref name=":3" />

Prior to the start of stage 15, the [[International Testing Agency]] tested Vingegaard early in the morning around 2am, with Pogačar tested around 5am. The tests took place outside of normal testing hours, with it later emerging that these and other late-night tests had been authorised by a Paris prosecutor.<ref name=":9">{{Cite news |last=Whittle |first=Jeremy |date=2026-07-20 |title=Vingegaard’s and Pogacar’s night-time doping tests authorised by Paris judge |url=https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/jul/20/tadej-pogacar-jonas-vingegaard-night-time-doping-tests-authorised-paris-judge-tour-de-france-cycling |access-date=2026-07-26 |work=The Guardian |language=en-GB |issn=0261-3077}}</ref> Reacting to the tests, Vingegaard stated that "It’s good that they test, but when it’s affecting performance and your sleep, I don’t think it’s so good.”<ref name=":9" /> Evenepoel criticised the tests, stating that it was disrespectful and "something we [...] should not accept as athletes".<ref name=":10">{{Cite news |last=Whittle |first=Jeremy |date=19 July 2026 |title=Vingegaard crashes out of Tour de France after ‘inhuman’ 2am doping control |url=https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/jul/19/jonas-vingegaard-crashes-out-tour-de-france-remco-evenepoel-wins-stage-15 |access-date=27 July 2026 |work=The Guardian}}</ref>

Stage 15 took the race into the [[Savoy Prealps|Savoyard Alps]], with a finish at [[Plateau de Solaison]]. With about {{convert|24|km|mi|abbr=on}} remaining in the stage, Vingeegaard crashed exiting a roundabout, hitting the kerb. He abandoned the race, with news later emerging that he had broken his collarbone.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.cyclingweekly.com/racing/tour-de-france/luckily-its-only-a-broken-collarbone-jonas-vingegaard-on-crashing-out-of-tour-de-france|title='Luckily, it's only a broken collarbone' – Jonas Vingegaard on crashing out of Tour de France|first=Adam|last=Becket|date=July 20, 2026|accessdate=July 20, 2026|website=cyclingweekly.com|publisher=[[Cycling Weekly]]}}</ref> Merlier also abandoned during this stage, albeit due to the challenging terrain rather than injury. On the climb to the finish at Plateau de Solaison, Pogačar led Del Toro and Evenepoel as Seixas and Lipowitz lost time behind. In the finish, Evenepoel outsprinted Pogačar for the line to take his first mountain stage victory at the Tour de France. Following the stage, Pogačar stated that Vingegaard’s 2am drug test would have "ruined his deep sleep and then completely ruined the night", noting that this could have caused Vingegaard’s crash. Pogačar did note that "if this is necessary to still prove that we are riding clean, then I totally accept it".<ref name=":102">{{Cite news |last=Whittle |first=Jeremy |date=19 July 2026 |title=Vingegaard crashes out of Tour de France after ‘inhuman’ 2am doping control |url=https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/jul/19/jonas-vingegaard-crashes-out-tour-de-france-remco-evenepoel-wins-stage-15 |access-date=27 July 2026 |work=The Guardian}}</ref>

