== Stage 16 ==
;21 July 2026 – [[Évian-les-Bains]] to [[Thonon-les-Bains]], {{convert|26.1|km|abbr=on}} (ITT)
Stage 16 was the only [[individual time trial]] of the 2026 edition of the Tour, {{convert|26.1|km|abbr=on}} from [[Évian-les-Bains]] to [[Thonon-les-Bains]], with a second-category climb of the Côte de Larringes (9.7&nbsp;km at an average gradient of 4.3%) located in the first third of the course.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Stage 16 - Évian-les-Bains > Thonon-les-Bains - Tour de France 2026 |url=https://www.letour.fr/en/stage-16 |access-date=2026-07-05 |website=www.letour.fr |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite book |title=2026 Tour de France Roadbook |publisher=Amaury Sport Organisation |pages=158, 161}}</ref>

Evenepoel set the fastest time, winning a Tour time trial stage for the third time in his career. Pogačar was second, 28 seconds slower than Evenepoel, with his lead now 4 and a half minutes. Third on the stage was [[Mattias Skjelmose]] ({{UCI team code|LTK men|2026|nolink=y}}), over a minute slower than Evenepoel. In the fight for third overall in {{abbr|GC|general classification}}, Seixas beat del Toro, cutting the gap between them to around 20 seconds. Lipowitz crashed on the descent, breaking his collarbone and abandoning the race. Ayuso therefore moved into 5th overall on {{abbr|GC|general classification}}.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Whittle |first=Jeremy |date=2026-07-21 |title=Evenepoel pips Pogacar again as Tour de France night-time doping test row deepens |url=https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/jul/21/remco-evenepoel-tadej-pogacar-tour-de-france-nightime-doping-test-row-cycling |access-date=2026-07-27 |work=The Guardian |language=en-GB |issn=0261-3077}}</ref>

