== Stage 18 ==
;23 July 2026 – [[Voiron]] to [[Orcières-Merlette]], {{convert|185.2|km|abbr=on}}
[[File:TDF 2026 à Sassenage - 03 - A6301918 (cropped).jpg|thumb|Peloton in [[Sassenage]]]]
Remaining in the French Alps, the eighteenth stage gradually climbed from [[Voiron]] to a summit finish at [[Orcières-Merlette]] over a {{convert|185.2|km|abbr=on}} course. The stage included five categorised climbs – the first-category Côte d'Engins (11.4&nbsp;km at an average gradient of 5.4%), followed by two third-category climbs and a second-category climb, before the first-category ascent to the summit finish at Orcières-Merlette (7.1&nbsp;km at an average gradient of 6.7%, with the finish at an elevation of {{convert|1825|m|ft|abbr=on}}).<ref>{{Cite web |title=Stage 18 - Voiron > Orcières-Merlette - Tour de France 2026 |url=https://www.letour.fr/en/stage-18 |access-date=2026-07-05 |website=www.letour.fr |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite book |title=2026 Tour de France Roadbook |publisher=Amaury Sport Organisation |pages=174, 176, 179}}</ref>

A large breakaway went away, with strong climbers as well as Pedersen present. Pedersen took maximum points at the intermediate sprint, extending his lead to thirty-two points. On the climbs, the breakaway slowly diminished as [[Valentin Paret-Peintre]] ({{UCI team code|QST|2026|nolink=y}}) tried to gain points in the mountains classification. In the final climb however, Carapaz was the strongest rider, breaking away from the remaining four riders with {{convert|3.5|km|abbr=on}} to go, taking the stage win and the lead in the mountains classification. {{abbr|GC|general classification}} contenders finished together, although there was some concern that {{UCI team code|UEX|2026|nolink=y}} were suffering from illness, with Pogačar's key lieutenant [[Brandon McNulty]] abandoning the race.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Ostinek |first=Dani |date=2026-07-23 |title=Tour de France: Richard Carapaz flies solo across the final kilometres to land stunning mountaintop victory on stage 18 |url=https://www.cyclingnews.com/pro-cycling/racing/tour-de-france-richard-carapaz-flies-solo-across-the-final-kilometres-to-land-stunning-mountaintop-victory-on-stage-18/ |access-date=2026-07-28 |website=Cyclingnews |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Whittle |first=Jeremy |date=2026-07-23 |title=Tour de France worries emerge for Tadej Pogacar after illness sweeps through team |url=https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/jul/23/tour-de-france-stage-18-report-tadej-pogacar-team-illness-richard-carapaz |access-date=2026-07-28 |work=The Guardian |language=en-GB |issn=0261-3077}}</ref>

