== Stage 19 ==
;24 July 2026 – [[Gap, Hautes-Alpes|Gap]] to [[Alpe d'Huez]], {{convert|127.9|km|abbr=on}}
[[File:Alpe_d'Huez,_France_(7957045090).jpg|thumb|Stage 19 finished at the top of [[Alpe d'Huez]]; the climb is {{convert|13.8|km|1|abbr=on}} long,  an average gradient of 7.9% and features 21 [[hairpin turns]].]]
Heading north, the nineteenth stage took riders from [[Gap, Hautes-Alpes|Gap]] to a summit finish at [[Alpe d'Huez]] over a {{convert|127.9|km|abbr=on}} course. The stage included four categorised climbs – two second-category climbs, the first category [[Col du Noyer]] (7.2&nbsp;km at an average gradient of 8.5%) and the ''hors catégorie'' ascent to the summit finish at Alpe d'Huez (13.8&nbsp;km at an average gradient of 8.1%, with the finish at an elevation of {{convert|1850|m|ft|abbr=on}}).<ref>{{Cite web |title=Stage 19 - Gap > Alpe d'Huez - Tour de France 2026 |url=https://www.letour.fr/en/stage-19 |access-date=2026-07-05 |website=www.letour.fr |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite book |title=2026 Tour de France Roadbook |publisher=Amaury Sport Organisation |pages=184, 186, 188-189}}</ref> 

Tadej Pogačar eclipsed Marco Pantani's Alpe d'Huez record, set in 1995.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Farrand |first=Stephen |date=2026-07-24 |title=Tadej Pogačar smashes 30-year-old Alpe d'Huez climbing record set by Marco Pantani |url=https://www.cyclingnews.com/pro-cycling/teams-riders/tadej-pogacar-beats-nearly-30-year-old-alpe-dhuez-climbing-record-set-by-marco-pantani/ |access-date=2026-07-27 |website=Cyclingnews |language=en}}</ref>

