== Stage 21 ==
;26 July 2026 – [[Paris]] ([[Champs-Élysées stage in the Tour de France|Champs-Élysées]]) to Paris (Champs-Élysées), {{convert|88.7|km|abbr=on}}
[[File:Étape 21 Tour France 2026 Rue Saint Éleuthère - Paris XVIII (FR75) - 2026-07-26 - 3.jpg|thumb|[[Mads Pedersen]], [[Tadej Pogačar]] and eventual stage winner [[Mathieu van der Poel]] on the Montmartre climb]]
The twenty-first stage was originally scheduled to be contested over {{convert|132.5|km|abbr=on}}, from [[Thoiry, Yvelines|Thoiry]] to [[Paris]]. However, due to a redeployment of security staff to the [[Gironde]] department following [[2026 France wildfires|wildfires]], the stage was shortened by {{convert|43.8|km|abbr=on}}.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.letour.fr/en/stage-21|title=Stage 21|work=[[Tour de France]]|publisher=[[Amaury Sport Organisation]]|accessdate=25 July 2026|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260724055122/https://www.letour.fr/en/stage-21|archivedate=24 July 2026}}</ref> All pre-stage activities were held in [[Thoiry, Yvelines|Thoiry]], before a bus transfer to Paris, with the stage commencing on the Champs-Élysées.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.letour.fr/en/news/2026/change-to-the-route-of-the-final-stage-1/1355402|title=Change to the route of the final stage|accessdate=25 July 2026|date=25 July 2026|work=[[Tour de France]]|publisher=[[Amaury Sport Organisation]]}}</ref> The stage used the [[Montmartre]] circuit first used at the [[2024 Summer Olympics|Paris 2024 Summer Olympics]] and the [[2025 Tour de France]], with the traditional finish line located on the [[Champs-Élysées stage in the Tour de France|Champs-Élysées]]. The stage had four fourth-category climbs, with three ascents of the Côte de la Butte Montmartre climb (1.1&nbsp;km at an average gradient of 6.5%).<ref name=":1">{{Cite web |title=Stage 21 - Thoiry > Paris Champs-Élysées - Tour de France 2026 |url=https://www.letour.fr/en/stage-21 |access-date=2026-07-05 |website=www.letour.fr |language=en}}</ref><ref name=":5">{{Cite book |title=2026 Tour de France Roadbook |publisher=Amaury Sport Organisation |pages=208, 211, 213}}</ref> With {{convert|11|km|abbr=on}} from the final summit of the climb to the finish line on the Champs-Élysées, it was considered that sprinters would have a greater chance of contending for the stage victory.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Lamoureux |first=Lyne |last2= |first2= |last3= |date=2026-06-08 |title=Tour de France 2026 stage 21 preview |url=https://www.cyclingnews.com/pro-cycling/racing/tour-de-france-2026-stage-21-preview/ |access-date=2026-07-05 |website=Cyclingnews |language=en}}</ref>

